    "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. q-156854: 2x x'=8y' gives x'=1/8. q-156756: e^x x'-sin(y)y'=0 gives y'=3. Its solution incorrectly rewrites the original equation with right-hand side 0 instead of 1; differentiation and the final answer remain correct. q-157100: y=1 gives x=2, so 12x'=20 and x'=5/3. q-115951: y=0 gives x=0, so -3=2y' and y'=-3/2. q-157223: the first-quadrant condition gives x=4, so 8x'=12 and x'=3/2. q-48523: 2πrr'=(1/3)(2r') gives r=1/(3π), using the stipulated positive rate of increase. q-116650: r'=-24π/(12π)=-2 km/year, hence C'=-4π km/year; the requested rate of decrease is the positive magnitude 4π km/year. q-103781: the balloon height is 3 km and 3y'=5(12), giving 20 km/h. q-2939: the separation is 1 km and 0.8x'+0.6(-60)=20, giving 70 km/h. q-30080: at t=2, x=6, y=8, z=10, x'=3 and y'=8, so z'=(18+64)/10=8.2 ft/s. Its intermediate label of 10 mi is erroneous; the distance is 10 ft and the final units are correct. q-12451: dividing the sine series by π gives x-π²x³/6 as the first two nonzero terms. q-44625: x(x-5)>0 outside its roots, excluding both endpoints. q-116194: (x+4)(2x-1)≥0 outside its roots, including both endpoints. q-18862: polynomial division gives x²+4x+3=(x+1)(x+3). q-112651: division by (x-5) twice gives x²+9; the worked solution's intermediate denominator x-2 is an authored error and must be x-5. q-124201: (1/2)∫₀^π e^(2θ+2)dθ=e²(e^(2π)-1)/4. There is no supplied earlier submission or grade to reconcile; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions and independent calculations. The noted source errors do not change any final answer.",
